Sadruddin Rejeb wrote:
> 
> Hello there,
> Do you know if there's any compatibility-benchmarks list of em86? I'd
> like to know if SVGAlib programs can work under it, and also emulators
> (anyone tried snes9x?).

I haven't tested any SVGAlib programs yet.  I'm not positive if an
emulated x86 SVGA library would work on Alpha.  Unlike X, SVGAlib
talks directly to the VGA hardware.  The thunking to the native Alpha
version may be needed before this all works.

> Also, I'd like to know if anyone who bought an Alpha 21164PC with a SX
> motherboard is pleased with it (why is it so cheap compared to
> the LX?). Thanks for your attention,

Mainly because the SX is based on a less-expensive chip, the 21164PC
(the LX is based on the 21164).  The LX has the L2 cache on-chip and
an L3 cache on the motherboard.  The SX eliminates the L2 cache from
the chip and puts it on the motherboard; there is no L3 cache.  The
SX also is only certified to operate up to 533MHz; the LX can go up
to 600MHz.

