> > As an aside, does anyone know if there's a legal problem (it doesn't
> > bother me if there is, but I am curious) with making statically linked
> > executables on a OSF1 machine (source entirely authored by me), and
> > then distributing them over the Internet?
> 
> I would guess not, but you never know. DEC distributes their compiler
> for NT x86, and I'm sure it doesn't have such a limitation, but who
> knows what's in the fine print for their DU compilers.

I don't have any firm answers here, but I *do* know that this is a
legally sticky area.  The basic problem is that statically-linked
DU binaries *do* contain licensed library code.  Until Linux/Alpha
came along, distributing such binaries was not considered a problem
because it was *only* possible to run such binaries on another DU
system, for which the appropriate license fees had presumably been
paid.

Now that there is a freeware platform that can run DU binaries, the
issue is not nearly so clear-cut...

