Organization: The World @ Software Tool & Die
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha


"Sarah Addams" <Sarah.Addams@telergy.com> writes:
> Is the Alpha version of Linux 64 bit?

Yes it is.  Specifically, the programming model used in C is:

	char		8 bits
	short		16 bits
	int		32 bits
	long		64 bits
	void *		64 bits
	float		32 bits
	double		64 bits

This is the same model used by Digital UNIX.

> Does it significantly improve on the max number of files per process as
> compared with other Unixes? I believe 255 is a typical maximum...

The 2.0 kernel has a pretty hard limit of 256 on both Intel and Alpha.  

The 2.1 kernel changes this to 1024.  If you need more, you can bump
this constant in include/linux/fs.h and build a new kernel.  You'll
need to rebuild your application as well, and you may (I'm not sure)
need to rebuild libc from source as well...


