The answer is yes; this is a known bug, and the solution is to get hold of a
later version of f2c. I wish RedHat would make an RPM for a later version of 
f2c on all their platforms.

Their is some discussion of the problems with the Alpha version of f2c in the
RedHat distribution in the axp-list mailing list on the RedHat site. Apparently
that early version of f2c had not correctly taken into account the fact that,
on the Alpha, the pointer length is 64 bits while the default integer length
is 32 bits. Somewhere the implicit assumption is made that these 2 lengths
are the same. Later versions of f2c (I am led to believe) correct this error.

                                               Don Sinclair.  





